From 860b3146fd10ffab34e3e0db608fd6e63c4068fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam <sam@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:29:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vscode): make Windows activation failures visible and
 bundle win-ca

The activation error was logged only to the extension host console, and the 'View Logs' button called continue.viewLogs before that command existed, so clicking it did nothing. Write the real stack to ~/.continue/logs/activation-error.log, open a Continue Activation output channel and show the error text in the notification.

Also load system-ca dynamically (its top-level import is not Windows-safe), replace win-ca's dynamic ./crypt32-<arch> require with a loader that uses the copied out/crypt32-<arch>.node binding, and copy that native file in prepackage. Real VS Code 1.95 on win32-x64 now activates successfully.
